      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Enrich OpenObserve alerts with log context and notify responders through Novu\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow starts when a selected OpenObserve alert fires, normalizes the alert payload, and searches OpenObserve for relevant log context around the alert time. It selects the closest log event, optionally expands the surrounding context, then builds an incident brief. Before notifying responders through Novu, it checks a Data Table cooldown to suppress duplicates, supports a preview-only path, and records/report the notification outcome.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the OpenObserve trigger with the alert or monitor that should start the workflow.\n- Add OpenObserve credentials to both search nodes and verify the configured log stream, service field, default service, and search window match your environment.\n- Create or select the n8n Data Table used to store notification cooldown state, and ensure the load/save nodes point to it consistently.\n- Configure the Novu node with the correct Novu credentials, workflow/template, subscriber or topic, and payload fields expected by your notification template.\n- Review the preview-only and cooldown settings before enabling live responder notifications.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the enrichment configuration, log search window, anchor-selection logic, cooldown duration, and Novu payload/template to fit each service or incident severity."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
